   revenues. The results provide strong evidence of the flypaper effect,
   indicating that transfers from the Municipal Participation Fund (FPM),
   the State Tax on the Circulation of municipal spending, particularly
   among municipalities with lower expenditure levels. Regarding fiscal
   effort, the findings offer partial support for the Veil of Oates
   Hypothesis, as FPM transfers revenue generation. These findings advance
   the fiscal federalism literature by demonstrating that},
